          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curves"} algebraic curves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            is a sort of space of parameters parametrizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curves"} algebraic curves
            of given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
          %p
            %a{:href => "#DeligneMumford69"} Deligne-Mumford 69
            a nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactification
            of a moduli space of Riemann surfaces of fixed genus which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+compactification"} Deligne-Mumford compactification
          %p
            There is also a decorated version of curves with marked points, and of the corresponding compactified moduli space of stable curves of genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            marked points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{g,n}
            which plays an important role in the mathematical study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gromov-Witten+invariants"} Gromov-Witten invariants
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
          %p
            The special case of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n =1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mi ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,1}= \mathcal{M}_{ell}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#OverTheComplexNumbers Over the complex numbers
          #EquivalentlyModuliOfAlmostComplexStructures.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              On 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
              is integrable and hence is already a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "complex+structure#In2dAnyAlmostComplexStructureIsIntegrable"} this proposition
            %p
              Hence the moduli space of complex surfaces is also equivalent to just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+orbifold"} quotient orbifold
              of the space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structures"} almost complex structures
              by the orientation-preserving part of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
          %p
            This is reviewed for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Madsen07"}> Madsen 07, section 1.1
            ).
          #InTermsOfTheHigherToposOfSmoothStacks.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              We indicate how via remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalentlyModuliOfAlmostComplexStructures"}
              the moduli space of complex curves has a formulation in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy-type theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "complex+structure#InTermsOfSmoothStacks"} this remark
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of a
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              is modulated by a map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_X \;\colon\;  X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}GL(2n,\mathbb{R})
            %p
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stacks"} smooth stacks
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is equivalently a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi J
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi GL
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi τ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi almComp
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi GL
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp; \stackrel{J}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(n,\mathbb{C})
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\tau}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{almComp}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} GL(2n,\mathbb{R})
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p This in turn is equivalently a map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi almComp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J \;\colon\; \tau_X \longrightarrow almComp
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(2n,\mathbb{R})}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi SmthMfd
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                      %mi et
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_{(-)} \;\colon\; SmthMfd_{2n}^{et} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(2n,\mathbb{R})}
            %p
              of the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
              between them understood, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi almComp
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} almComp \in \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}GL(2n,\mathbb{R})}
              is the universal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structures"} almost complex structures
            %p
              Now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_X
              carries a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi almComp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\tau_X, almComp]//Diff(X)
            %p
              by a general abstract construction that is discussed in some detail at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "general+covariance#InHomotopyTypeTheory"} general covariant – Formalization in homotopy type theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n =1
              this is hence the Riemann moduli space.
          %h3#HomotopyTypeAndCohomology Homotopy type and cohomology
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the Riemann moduli spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_g
            (i.e. of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            is fully known only for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \leq 4
          %p
            However, in a stable range it has been fully computed in (
            %a{:href => "#MadsenWeiss02"}> Madsen-Weiss 02
            ), proving what was previously
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectured
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mumford%27s+conjecture"} Mumford's conjecture
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Madsen07"} Madsen 07
          %h3#OrbifoldEulerCharacteristic Orbifold Euler characteristic
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{g,1}
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            at negative integral values as follows (
            %a{:href => "#ZagierHarer86"}> Zagier-Harer 86
            ):
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mn 2
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\mathcal{M}_{g,1}) = \zeta(1-2g)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the expression of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            at negative integral values by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernoulli+numbers"} Bernoulli numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\mathcal{M}_{g,1}) = -\frac{B_{2g}}{2g}
                  \\,.
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            (once punctured complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tori"} tori
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 12
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi(\mathcal{M}_{1,1}) = -\frac{1}{12}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli space of elliptic curves
          %h3#relation_to_teichmller_space Relation to Teichmüller space
          %p
            Over the complex number then the moduli space of curves is a quotient of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teichm%C3%BCller+space"} Teichmüller space
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HubbardKoch13"} Hubbard-Koch 13
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#_
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 0
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Riemann mapping theorem
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Riemann+mapping+theorem"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{0,0}\simeq \ast
            is the point.
          %h3#__2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,0} \simeq \mathbb{R}^2
          %h3#__3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,1} = \mathcal{M}_{ell}
            , the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
          %h3#__4
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \geq 2
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\geq 2
            the moduli stack of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structures"} complex structures
            is equivalently that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+metrics"} hyperbolic metrics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+geometry"} hyperbolic geometry
            is used in the study of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{g \geq 2, n}
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"}> moduli space
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enumerative+geometry"} enumerative geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mumford+class"} Mumford class
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+super+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of super Riemann surfaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+%28higher%29+line+bundles"} moduli space of (higher) line bundles
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+conjecture"} Witten conjecture
          %h2#references References
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#DeligneMumford69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"} David Mumford
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The irreducibility of the space of curves of given genus
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/numdam-bin/fitem?id=PMIHES_1969__36__75_0"} numdam
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"}> David Mumford
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards an enumerative geometry of the moduli space of curves
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=85j:14046"} MR85j:14046
          %p
            On
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+curves"} moduli spaces of curves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces+of+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli spaces of Riemann surfaces
            with emphasis on their
            = succeed "-structure:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
          %ul
            %li
              Lizhen Ji,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shing-Tung+Yau"} Shing-Tung Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %em Transformation Groups and Moduli Spaces of Curves
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/pages/books/items/00000353/index.php"} ISBN:9781571462237
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            of the moduli stack is in
          %ul
            %li
              John Harer,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The cohomology of the moduli space of curves
          %p
            The stable rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+cohomology"} orbifold cohomology
            of the moduli stack was computed in
          %ul
            %li#MadsenWeiss02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"}> Ib Madsen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Weiss"} Michael Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The stable moduli space of Riemann surfaces:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mumford%27s+conjecture"} Mumford's conjecture
              %strong 165
              (2007), no. 3, 843–941,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2009b:14051"} MR2009b:14051
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.4007/annals.2007.165.843"} doi
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0212321"} math.AT/0212321
          %p exposition of this is in
          %ul
            %li#Madsen07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"}> Ib Madsen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Moduli spaces from a topological viewpoint
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.icm2006.org/proceedings/Vol_I/20.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Gabriele Mondello,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Combinatorial classes on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℳ
                            %mrow
                              %mi g
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{g,n}
                    are tautological
                %strong 44
                (2004), 2329-–2390,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2005g:14056"} MR2005g:14056
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1155/S1073792804131462"} doi
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0303207"} math.AG/0303207
            %li
              %p
                Gabriele Mondello,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Riemann surfaces, ribbon graphs and combinatorial classes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uniroma1.it/~mondello/me/papers/ober-definitive.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.1792"} math.AG/0705.1792
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2010f:32012"} MR2010f:32012
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+Hamilton"}> Alastair Hamilton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classes on compactifications of the moduli space of curves through solutions to the quantum master equation
                %strong 89
                (2009), no. 2, 115–130.
            %li
              %p
                %em The moduli of curves
                %a{:href => "http://www2.imperial.ac.uk/~acorti/download/moduli.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold+Euler+characteristic"} orbifold Euler characteristic
            of the moduli space of curves was originally computed in
          %ul
            %li#ZagierHarer86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Don+Zagier"}> Don Zagier
              , John Harer,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Euler characteristic of the moduli space of curves
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/143377"} EUDML
          %p
            The complex analytic structure and the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teichm%C3%BCller+space"} Teichmüller space
            is further discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HubbardKoch13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Hubbard"}> John Hubbard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sarah+Koch"} Sarah Koch
              %em An analytic construction of the Deligne-Mumford compactification of the moduli space of curves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.0062"}> arXiv:1301.0062
              )
          %p Reviews include
          %ul
            %li
              %em Mathematical ideas and notions in quantum field theory – 5. The Euler characteristic of the moduli space of curves
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EulerCharacteristicOfSpaceOfCurves.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+homotopy+type"} Étale homotopy type
            of moduli stacks of curves is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Paola Frediani, Frank Neumann,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Étale homotopy types of moduli stacks of algebraic curves with symmetries
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404387"} arXiv:math/0404387
        .revisedby
